<title>UK: UK Channel 5 costs soar to 180 mln stg - paper.</title>
<headline>UK Channel 5 costs soar to 180 mln stg - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pearson Plc is set to announce that the cost of retuning video recorders for Channel Five terrestrial television channel will be 180 million pounds, up from an orginal forecast of 55 million pounds, the Independent reported.</p>
<p>The newspaper said that the costs would be published in a trading statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Pearson has a 24 percent stake in Channel Five and its share of the costs could be 45 million pounds, the paper said.</p>
<p>Other shareholders in the venture are United News &amp; Media Plc, Warburg Pincus, the U.S. investment bank, and Luxembourg broadcaster CLT.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887  ))</p>
